b:
Currently, I've been playing in a group with a neutral cleric, barbarian and sorcerer. 

I am a chaotic good paladin with Oath fo Ancients. We capture and interrogate a lot of enemies. After I've used my array of face skills to milk them for info, I usually either offer to let them go if they leave forever and change their ways, or offer them a [CARDINAL] on [CARDINAL] duel to the death with our barbarian.

&amp;#x200B;

Sadly, I have been cut-off midway into their answer every time as each of the other party members has beheaded, skull crushed or vaporized them right in front of me, splattering their blood all over my face.

&amp;#x200B;

"Why do I even hang out with you guys..."

I think this sums up a lot of the appeal for some folks. Human is the most popular race in like, every game its an option. 

Theres inherently some charm to being just "a regular guy" in a wacky fantasy world and its a safe choice if you don't want to try and roleplay something drastically foreign. Like, RPing [PERSON] must be a trip.

&amp;#x200B;

[PERSON] is the only unbeatable WPVP class. Not because you win, but because you can bubblehearth away.

&amp;#x200B;

Unbeatable.
